  "antiflood.use_setfloodmode_lt_ban_kick_mute": "Use /setfloodmode &lt;ban|kick|mute|tban|tmute&gt; [duration].\ntban and tmute need a duration, like 30m, 2h, 3d or 1w.",
  "antiflood.use_setfloodtimer_lt_count_gt_lt": "Use /setfloodtimer &lt;count&gt; &lt;duration&gt;, for example /setfloodtimer 5 10s, or /setfloodtimer off.\nThe count is {MIN_COUNT} to {MAX_COUNT}; the duration is like 10s, 2m or 1h (up to 24 hours).",
  "antiraid.a_raid_now_lasts": "A raid now lasts <b>{duration_text}</b>.",
  "antiraid.a_raid_now_starts_when_accounts": "A raid now starts when <b>{joins}</b> accounts join within <b>{duration_text}</b>.",
  "antiraid.about": "\nA raid is a crowd of new accounts joining a chat within moments, usually to flood it. With antiraid on, I count the joins: when too many come in a short time, the chat is in a raid for a while, and everybody who joins during it is dealt with, as are the people who made it a raid.\n\nBy default 10 joins within 1 minute make a raid, and a raid lasts 1 hour. Newcomers are muted until the raid is over (they can write once it ends), or kicked, or banned. Chat admins, approved users, bots and the bot's staff are never touched.\n\nAntiraid is off until a chat admin turns it on, and I need the right to restrict users.\n",
  "antiraid.antiraid_enabled_raid_joins_within_lasts": "<b>Antiraid</b>\n• <b>Enabled:</b> <code>{opt}</code>\n• <b>Raid:</b> <code>{joins}</code> joins within <code>{duration_text}</code>\n• <b>Lasts:</b> <code>{duration_text2}</code>\n• <b>Newcomers are:</b> <code>{mode_text}</code>",
  "antiraid.antiraid_is_on_but_i_can": "Antiraid is on, but I can't act: {exc}",
  "antiraid.during_a_raid_newcomers_are_now": "During a raid, newcomers are now <b>{mode_text}</b>.",
  "antiraid.help.how_long_a_raid_lasts": "How long a raid lasts, like 30m, 2h or 1d. Default: 1 hour.",
  "antiraid.help.how_many_joins_within_how": "How many joins within how much time make a raid. Example: /raidlimit 10 1m. Default: 10 within 1 minute.",
  "antiraid.help.turn_antiraid_on_or_off": "Turn antiraid on or off, or show its settings. Turning it off also ends a running raid.",
  "antiraid.help.what_happens_to_newcomers_during": "What happens to newcomers during a raid. Default: mute until the raid is over.",
  "antiraid.muted_until_the_raid_is_over": "muted until the raid is over",
  "antiraid.raid_detected_accounts_joined_within_for": "<b>Raid detected.</b> {people} accounts joined within {duration_text}. For the next {duration_text2}, newcomers are {mode_text}.",
  "antiraid.raid_running_ends_in": "\n• <b>Raid:</b> <code>running</code>, ends in <code>{duration_text}</code>",
  "antiraid.use_antiraid_on_or_antiraid_off": "Use /antiraid on or /antiraid off.",
  "antiraid.use_raidlimit_lt_joins_gt_lt": "Use /raidlimit &lt;joins&gt; &lt;time&gt;, with joins from {MIN_JOINS} to {MAX_JOINS} and a time like 30s, 1m or 10m. Example: /raidlimit 10 1m.",
  "antiraid.use_raidmode_lt_mute_kick_ban": "Use /raidmode &lt;mute|kick|ban&gt;.",
  "antiraid.use_raidtime_lt_time_gt_from": "Use /raidtime &lt;time&gt;, from 1 minute to 7 days, like 30m, 2h or 1d.",
  "approves.about": "\nApproved users are people you trust without making them admins. In the chat where they are approved, automatic measures leave them alone: locks, blacklists, antiflood, global bans, federation bans and anything similar I learn later.\n\nApproval is per chat and never stops an admin from banning, muting or warning someone by hand. Chat admins are already exempt, so they can't be approved. My own staff can be approved like anyone else.\n\nName the user by replying to their message, or with a @username or a numeric ID.\n",
