  "fun.roasts.00": "{t} has the energy of a loading bar stuck at 99%.",
  "fun.roasts.01": "{t} is proof that confidence and competence are two different things.",
  "fun.roasts.02": "{t} types like the keyboard owes them money.",
  "fun.roasts.03": "If {t} were a spice, they'd be unsalted flour.",
  "fun.roasts.04": "{t} brings the same energy to every chat: it arrives late and leaves early.",
  "fun.roasts.05": "{t} sends voice messages the way other people send threats.",
  "fun.roasts.06": "{t} reads the rules the way cats read instruction manuals.",
  "fun.roasts.07": "{t} is the human version of a link that opens in the wrong app.",
  "fun.roasts.08": "{t} argues like a browser tab: loud, and nobody knows where it's coming from.",
  "fun.roasts.09": "{t} has main-character energy and side-quest results.",
  "fun.roasts.10": "{t} is the reason the mute button exists. It's a compliment. Sort of.",
  "fun.roasts.11": "{t} has a battery life of 4% and still joins every conversation.",
  "fun.roasts.12": "{t} gives advice like a GPS recalculating: confident, and wrong.",
  "fun.roasts.13": "{t} is the kind of person who replies 'ok' to a paragraph of thoughts.",
  "fun.roasts.14": "{t} says 'one last thing' and then writes for another twenty minutes.",
  "fun.roasts.15": "{t} treats the pin button like a trophy case.",
  "fun.roasts.16": "{t} runs on caffeine, spite and about five unread messages.",
  "fun.roasts.17": "{t} has the confidence of a person who never scrolled up.",
  "fun.roasts.18": "{t} is like a software update: always at the wrong moment and nobody asked.",
  "fun.roasts.19": "{t} gets lost in a group chat with three people.",
  "fun.roasts.20": "{t} has opinions about everything and sources for nothing.",
  "fun.roasts.21": "{t} is the human equivalent of 'seen at 3:07'.",
  "fun.roasts.22": "{t} reads the room the way a printer reads a PDF: with great effort and no result.",
  "fun.roasts.23": "{t} is 80% typing indicator and 20% message.",
  "fun.roasts.24": "{t} writes 'brb' and returns the following week.",
  "fun.roasts.25": "{t} has a great future behind them.",
  "fun.roasts.26": "{t} is the type to say 'quick question' and then open a seminar.",
  "fun.roasts.27": "{t} has the same reaction time as a government website.",
  "fun.roasts.28": "{t} treats every chat like a stage and every message like an encore.",
  "fun.roasts.29": "{t} is a walking 'this meeting could have been an email'.",
  "fun.roasts.30": "{t} has strong Wi-Fi in the argument and weak signal in the facts.",
  "fun.roasts.31": "{t} brings snacks to a debate and leaves with a lesson.",
  "fun.roasts.32": "{t} replies to everything with a thumbs-up and a hidden sigh.",
  "fun.roasts.33": "{t} would lose a staring contest to a screensaver.",
  "fun.roasts.34": "{t} is like a loading spinner: busy, and I'm not sure for what.",
  "fun.roasts.35": "{t} reads the first line and replies to the fourth.",
  "fun.roasts.36": "{t} treats 'mute' as a personal challenge.",
  "fun.roasts.37": "{t} brings the energy of a Monday morning to a Friday night.",
  "fun.roasts.38": "{t} reacts to the chat with all the speed of a snail on holiday.",
  "fun.roasts.39": "{t} is the human version of a fake 'download now' button.",
  "fun.roasts.40": "{t} has more unread messages than friends.",
  "fun.roasts.41": "{t} is the reason the 'delete for everyone' button exists.",
  "fun.roasts.42": "{t} explains jokes the way instruction manuals explain nothing.",
  "fun.roasts.43": "{t} has the sleep schedule of a nocturnal bug and the opinions of a daytime talk show.",
  "fun.roasts.44": "{t} is like a keyboard shortcut nobody remembers: powerful in theory, useless in practice.",
  "fun.roasts.45": "{t} sends 'hello' and then goes offline for the weekend.",
  "fun.roasts.46": "{t} takes screenshots of conversations and never opens them again.",
  "fun.roasts.47": "{t} calls it 'a quick fix' and it takes three weeks.",
  "fun.roasts.48": "{t} is cheerful enough to be annoying and annoying enough to be missed.",
  "fun.roasts.49": "{t} still uses the word 'actually' like a weapon.",
