  "joinblacklists.about": "\nBlock people from joining when their profile contains certain words, which stops spammers before they post a single message. There are four lists, one for each part of a profile that is checked: the name, the @username, the bio and the personal channel (its name and its username). Each chat can have up to 10 triggers per list.\n\nSomeone who matches is banned and the \"joined\" message is removed. Bots, chat admins, approved users and the bot's staff are never blocked, and neither is anyone who was added by a chat admin.\n\nTriggers match whole words and ignore case, so \"casino\" catches \"Best Casino!\" but not \"casinos\". To catch a word inside a longer one, use a wildcard: *casino* matches @best_casino_bot. Write one trigger per line to add several at once.\n\nThe commands that change the lists are for chat admins with the right to change chat info. Anyone can look at them.\n",
  "joinblacklists.give_me_the_triggers_to_remove": "Give me the triggers to remove, one per line. Example: /unblacklist{kind} spam word",
  "joinblacklists.give_me_triggers_one_per_line": "Give me triggers, one per line. Example: /blacklist{kind} spam word",
  "joinblacklists.help.block_people_whose_bio_matches": "Block people whose bio matches the trigger.",
  "joinblacklists.help.block_people_whose_name_matches": "Block people whose name matches the trigger.",
  "joinblacklists.help.block_people_whose_personal_channel": "Block people whose personal channel (its name or its username) matches the trigger.",
  "joinblacklists.help.block_people_whose_username_matches": "Block people whose @username matches the trigger.",
  "joinblacklists.help.list_the_join_blacklists_of": "List the join blacklists of this chat. Alias: /joinblacklist.",
  "joinblacklists.help.remove_a_bio_trigger": "Remove a bio trigger.",
  "joinblacklists.help.remove_a_channel_trigger": "Remove a channel trigger.",
  "joinblacklists.help.remove_a_name_trigger": "Remove a name trigger.",
  "joinblacklists.help.remove_a_username_trigger": "Remove a username trigger.",
  "joinblacklists.join_blacklists_in": "<b>Join blacklists in {v}</b>",
  "joinblacklists.note.any_single_character_except_whitespace": "\n        ? - any single character except whitespace.\n        * - any run of characters except whitespace (great for URLs).\n        ** - any run of characters, whitespace included.\n        A backslash makes them literal: \\* and \\?\n        ",
  "joinblacklists.note.blacklistname_free_crypto_names_with": "\n        /blacklistname free crypto - names with the words \"free crypto\".\n        /blacklistusername *casino* - any username with casino inside.\n        /blacklistbio t.me/* - bios that link to a Telegram chat or channel.\n        /unblacklistbio t.me/*\n        ",
  "joinblacklists.the_list_is_full_triggers_remove": "The {kind} list is full ({MAX_PER_KIND} triggers). Remove one first.",
  "joinblacklists.there_are_none_yet_add_one": "{title}\n\nThere are none yet. Add one with /blacklistname, /blacklistusername, /blacklistbio or /blacklistchannel.",
  "joinblacklists.title": "Join Blacklists",
  "language.about": "\nI can speak English and Polish. The language belongs to the chat: each group has its own, and so does your private chat with me.\n\nNames of commands, log entries for developers and tags like #GBANNED stay in English.\n",
  "language.done_the_language_of_this_chat": "Done. The language of this chat is now <b>{language}</b>.",
  "language.help.show_the_language_of_this": "Show the language of this chat and let you change it, or give a code straight away: /setlang en or /setlang pl. In a group it needs the right to change chat info; in a private chat anyone can change their own.",
  "language.i_don_t_speak_that_use": "I don't speak that. Use one of: {codes}.",
  "language.the_language_of_this_chat_is": "The language of this chat is <b>{language}</b>.\n\nAvailable languages:\n{listing}\n\nPick one with the buttons below.",
  "language.title": "Language",
  "locks.about": "\nLock a kind of message and I delete every one of them: stickers, links, forwards, voice messages, a whole alphabet... Locks do not affect chat admins, approved users or the bot's staff, and edited messages are checked too. /locktypes explains every kind.\n\nLocks that catch links, forwards, commands, stickers and the like can be eased with the allowlist: whatever is on it stays allowed, so you can lock all links but let one site through.\n\nBy default I just delete. With /lockwarns on, whoever breaks a lock also gets a warn, and is punished at the warn limit (see /warnmode). With /lockmode you can pick a punishment instead: mute, ban, kick, or a timed mute or ban.\n\nEverything here is for chat admins with the right to change chat info.\n",
